{
  // Test-mode compilation config. Extends the production tsconfig but
  // includes test files (which the production config excludes).
  //
  // History: this config previously produced 103 cross-package rootDir
  // errors (TS6059 + TS6307). The audit's original write-up blamed
  // four production files that imported `SocialMemoryManager` via
  // relative paths, but the actual cascade was driven primarily by
  // `emotional-memory-llm-adapter.ts` importing from the memory
  // barrel (`'../../../memory/src/index'`), which dragged every
  // transitive export into cognition's compilation under the wrong
  // rootDir. Migrating that import plus the three `SocialMemoryManager`
  // imports to `@conscious-bot/memory` — after resolving a dual-class
  // naming collision in memory that previously blocked the migration —
  // closed all 103 errors. The `SocialMemoryManager` dual-class issue
  // was resolved by deleting the dead flat variant and re-pointing the
  // memory barrel at the nested survivor (see commit history).
  //
  // The `**/*.json` include entry below is load-bearing: three files
  // import JSON fixtures/schemas (scenario_line.schema.json,
  // envelope-golden-vectors.json, hash-parity-cases.json) and without
  // the glob, tsc reports TS6307 "not listed within the file list of
  // project" for each. The errors were pre-existing but drowned out
  // by the 103-error cascade; closing the cascade made them visible.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": [
    "src/**/*",
    "src/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/**/*.spec.ts",
    "src/**/*.json"
  ],
  "exclude": ["dist", "node_modules"]
}
